1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:09,000
Typical audited auctions open every bid to prove the price.
DarkCall proves the price without opening the bids, then settles in shielded ZEC.

2
00:00:09,000 --> 00:00:14,000
3 identical units · reserve 20 · deposit budget 100 zatoshi · bidding closes in 2 minutes.

3
00:00:14,000 --> 00:00:22,000
The bidder's client proves in zero knowledge that the bid commitment matches 3 secret shares,
one per operator. Operators check and sign. (Demo: the local helper sees the typed bid.)

4
00:00:22,000 --> 00:00:27,000
Bids 77, 61, 43 and 21 were typed for this demo. Nothing here shows or publishes them.

5
00:00:27,000 --> 00:00:30,000
Time cut · 1 min 56 s of real time — Bidding stays open until its real deadline.

6
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:35,000
The three operators sign the closed book. Clearing waits until every ticket is funded.

7
00:00:35,000 --> 00:00:40,000
Each ticket gets a real shielded deposit on an isolated NU7 regtest, into a 2-of-3 FROST escrow.

8
00:00:40,000 --> 00:00:43,000
Time cut · 1 min 49 s of real time — Deposits confirm; operators decrypt them and re-verify the same proofs and shares.

9
00:00:43,000 --> 00:00:49,000
4 deposits · 4 bid proofs + 12 share pairs re-verified · 12 receipts · book signed again over the same root.

10
00:00:49,000 --> 00:00:53,000
Three operators compute on secret shares (REP3) and jointly prove the result (coNoir).
No one reconstructs the bids.

11
00:00:53,000 --> 00:01:00,000
Proof verified in under 10 seconds. 3 of 3 units sold. The price is the highest losing bid;
who placed it, and every winner's bid, stay hidden.

12
00:01:00,000 --> 00:01:06,000
Ticket 01 opens only its own verified outcome: won, refund 79.

13
00:01:06,000 --> 00:01:11,000
One shielded transaction will pay the seller and refund all four bidders.

14
00:01:11,000 --> 00:01:14,000
Time cut · 15 min 01 s of real time — Six Halo2 output-binding proofs, the settlement proof, 2-of-3 FROST signing, Zebra acceptance, 2 confirmations, six wallet scans and the public check.

15
00:01:14,000 --> 00:01:21,000
Every output is bound to the proven result. A public verifier replays it with no secrets.

16
00:01:21,000 --> 00:01:28,000
Everyone: the price and a shielded transaction. Each bidder: only their own result.
Operators: winners and refunds, never the bid list.

17
00:01:28,000 --> 00:01:34,000
Ticket 01 decrypts its memo with its own viewing key: won, 79 zatoshi refunded.

18
00:01:34,000 --> 00:01:39,000
Ticket 04 decrypts its own memo: lost, the full 100 zatoshi refunded.

19
00:01:39,000 --> 00:01:45,000
Flip one byte of the receipt proof: the fixed verifier rejects it before the key is read.

20
00:01:45,000 --> 00:01:53,000
What this prototype assumes — Bid secrecy: at most one semi-honest corrupt operator (REP3). Custody: 2-of-3 FROST; two colluding signers can move funds. Operators learn winners and refunds. The price is the highest losing bid. Demo: all parties on one machine; the local helper sees typed bids. Isolated NU7 regtest, not testnet or mainnet.

21
00:01:53,000 --> 00:01:59,000
Verify it yourself — scripts/docker_verify.sh Builds every pinned tool from committed source in a clean Linux container, verifies every committed settlement and rejects a tampered proof.
